Yes, 14 Mill Wynd is in the Glenarrow Town Centre conservation area. It is not a listed building and has no tree preservation order.

Under the council's window guidance, replacing windows in a conservation area needs a planning application unless the new windows match the existing ones in material and pattern. If you want to change the material or the design (for example, switching to uPVC or altering the glazing pattern), you should apply before starting work.

I can't give a formal opinion on whether your specific proposal would be approved. If you tell me what you have in mind, I can check the guidance further, or if you have an existing application reference, I can look up its status.
